{
  "name": "notifications-det (Settings > Notifications: seeded channels, notified events and recent sends; create det-auto-channel, edit and delete through the row menu, test, errors; developer mode off and on; every step green)",
  "stopOnError": false,
  "notes": [
    "The section lives in the settings window: every pass enters it through settings-nav-notifications, and re-entering it (settings-nav-general then back) remounts it, which is how the once-stub on list_notification_channels reaches the mount and renders the channel error with its Disclosure while the notified events stay settable.",
    "Edit and Delete sit in the row menu (channel-menu-<id>): the menu is opened before channel-edit-btn-<id> or channel-delete-btn-<id> is clicked.",
    "The technical identifier and the headers of a web call sit in collapsed Disclosures; their toggle buttons (disc-technical-id-toggle, <prefix>-headers-disclosure-toggle) are clicked before the fields are asserted.",
    "The test of a channel ends on an outcome the seeded HOME does not fix (a native notification may or may not be shown): the step sleeps and captures rather than asserting success or failure."
  ],
